{
  "_comment": [
    "Copy the 'hooks' block into .claude/settings.json (shared, committed) or",
    ".claude/settings.local.json (per-machine, gitignored). Merge it with any",
    "hooks already configured -- this file is an example, not a drop-in replacement.",
    "Paths are relative to the repo root, which is the working directory hooks run in.",
    "On Windows use 'python' instead of 'python3'.",
    "Both scripts always exit 0 and never write to stdout, so they can never deny a",
    "tool call or stop a session; see .claude/hooks/README.md.",
    "",
    "No SessionStart entry is configured here on purpose: the kit ships facts-layer",
    "hooks only, and a session-start script runs host commands and injects host text.",
    "The two patterns -- instruction injection, and the provisioning skeleton with its",
    "DEGRADED accumulator and hook-install-as-step-0 -- are written out with fragments",
    "in .claude/hooks/README.md. Add a SessionStart block here once you have written",
    "the scripts, alongside the three blocks below."
  ],
  "hooks": {
    "PreToolUse": [
      {
        "matcher": "*",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "python3 .claude/hooks/tool_use.py",
            "timeout": 10
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "PostToolUse": [
      {
        "matcher": "*",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "python3 .claude/hooks/tool_use.py",
            "timeout": 10
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "SubagentStop": [
      {
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "python3 .claude/hooks/subagent_stop.py",
            "timeout": 15
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}
